Z||000000||fiero56||12-08-2000||04:16 PM||||Why do we do this to ourselves? We get interested in these little cars, and after a bit of time we own mutiple Fieros. During my 1 1/2 week absence it turns out the water pump on my Formula leaked all over the garage floor. I bought another and will probably install it tonight. Right now I am rebuilding the headlights motors for my '86 SE as I sit here. I also have to install the housings and motors, the heater core for the SE needs to be installed, the upper ball joints and throttle cable for the Formula arrived last week, still need to be installed. And that is just the stuff I have ready to be replaced/fixed. The Formula still needs and engine rebuild, I need to find the cause of high idle on the SE, and the rear brakes on the Formula still need to be replaced. <P>All this fuss, and I am still always on the lookout for a third. Seems the 150,000 mile mark is exactly when everything on a vehicle(no matter what car) goes bad. I've seen it on all sorts of cars. The Fiero is no exception. Maybe I should sell the SE before it hits 150K miles. That gives me 48K miles left of fun with it.||||reg||2
Z||000001||BOILERMAKER||12-08-2000||06:53 PM||||Just the nature of the beast.  I have been there quite a few times over the past couple of years.  Seems when one thing goes, the rest go with it.  Good thing we are all in the same boat.||||reg||1
